35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the tender records show plant costs rising, but inspection-driven work stays on schedule. Comfort projects slip.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Wow, that’s a huge cost! And specialist rooms are mostly empty while general ones are always full. We really need to balance that!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Yumi, empty specialist rooms don’t solve my problem. My technicians are drowning in manual checks. We need relief, not more empty space.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, your burden is real, but my data shows single-wing projects fail. We must prioritize shared spaces to ensure actual user satisfaction.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, a fifth rise in plant costs with no reserve? That’s not a budget, it’s a slow leak. We’re funding the leak, not the building.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that slow leak worries me. If we don’t fix the reserve, the schedule will slip again, just as I feared.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@George, I hear you! But if we build general rooms, maybe fewer people need specialist ones? Let’s see if that eases your load!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, general rooms won’t stop the manual checks. My technicians are stuck with outdated equipment. We need to fix the tools, not just the rooms.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I understand the strain. But my data proves single-wing projects disappoint users. We must build shared spaces to ensure satisfaction, not just fix tools.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, you’re right. The reserve gap means we’re buying expensive plant that will fail without maintenance. We need to fund the repair, not just the ribbon-cutting.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, shared spaces sound lovely, but if the plant costs keep rising, we’ll just be maintaining a bigger, more expensive mess.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, shared spaces are great, but my data shows general rooms are already overflowing! We need to fix the imbalance first, not just add more!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, shared spaces won’t stop the manual labor. My technicians are exhausted. We must address the staffing gap before adding more rooms.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, @George, I hear you. But my survey data shows older blocks are hazardous. We must avoid those delays. Shared spaces are the only viable path forward.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, hazardous blocks are a liability, not a feature. We can’t build shared spaces on a foundation of unpriced decay.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, I hear your concern about safety. But if we ignore the rising plant costs, the schedule will slip again, leaving us with unfinished, hazardous spaces.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, I agree safety is key! But my booking data shows general rooms are overflowing. We must fix that imbalance before adding new shared spaces!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, I respect your caution, but my technicians are already stretched thin. Adding shared spaces without fixing the staffing gap will just break them.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, @Yumi, I hear your concerns. But my data proves shared spaces satisfy users, while single-wing projects fail. We must prioritize shared spaces to ensure actual satisfaction.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, satisfaction is cheap if the building collapses. We must price the decay before we promise the joy.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
